# L §4.4 (tally 2.1.8 R13, X2; K1, T's fixes/g6b/b2): a window read through a same row is a copy and keeps its
# name, a; windows each takes a day by day. The same lines as 2.1.7's refcore.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input a: date
input b: date


version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-03) "s"

version sm
  cite s
  known 2026-01-02
  same a = b
ask q2p: a
ask q2: a windows each
=== expect
q2 [a = 2026-03-01]: 2026-03-01
  cut 2026-06-30
q2 [a = 2026-03-02]: 2026-03-02
  cut 2026-06-30
q2 [a = 2026-03-03]: 2026-03-03
  cut 2026-06-30
q2p: window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-03)
  cut 2026-06-30
warning: WARN-UNREAD input b is read by nothing
